<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-7">7 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Frederick Barbarossa's crusaders defeat the Seljuks of Rum at Philomelion</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> defeated the Turkish army of the Sultanate of Rûm at Philomelion. The victory came on the emperor's march during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, in the year of his death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksehir">Philomelion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-10">10 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Frederick Barbarossa drowns on the Third Crusade</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> drowned in the Saleph river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> while leading his army to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>. Much of the German crusading force broke up after his death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-24">24 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Conrad of Montferrat becomes King of Jerusalem by marriage</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a>, who had held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, married Isabella I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and so became de facto King of Jerusalem. He was officially elected king only in April 1192, days before his murder.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tryavna">Battle of Tryavna</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tryavna was fought in 1190 in a pass of the Balkan Mountains near Tryavna, in present-day Bulgaria.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-schwabisch-hall">Diet of Schwäbisch Hall</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Diet of Schwäbisch Hall was an imperial assembly held in 1190 at Schwäbisch Hall in Swabia under King Henry VI.</p></div></li></ol></section>
